  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_050: multimodal/multiprofile/scvi_n200/imagenet_vit_l/transformer/concat at 72.1% acc), the evidence is sparse and we need to reduce uncertainty about which design choices are most impactful. Config_010 is a minimal, controlled change from config_050—only the fusion strategy shifts from concat to weighted—while keeping all other components identical. This directly tests whether weighted fusion can outperform simple concatenation for combining the transformer-aggregated RNA and image features. It is the best use of experiment 2 because it is low-risk (a small perturbation of the current best), provides a clean A/B comparison on one axis, and if weighted fusion improves accuracy, it opens a productive family of weighted-fusion configs to exploit in subsequent experiments; if it does not, we confirm concat is the right choice and can pivot to testing other axes (image encoder, aggregation, profile setting) with greater confidence."
